    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d324">

                <pb facs="0647" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg637"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 916.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 22, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have your despatch of April 8, No. 653,
                    which relates to the proceedings at Mauritius, in the matter of the cargo of the
                    Sea Bride. It will be well, I think, to defer a representation on that subject
                    until a season more propitious than the present one.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
